WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.280
On-site assessment compares the forecast with actual conditions at the place and time of flight.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.400
Record wind direction, average behavior, gusts, temperature, visibility, precipitation, clouds,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.460
sun, and signs of change.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.108
Observe terrain and structures.

00:00:14.108 --> 00:00:16.992
Flags, trees, water, dust, smoke, drifting precipitation,

00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:19.876
and cloud movement can reveal local effects.

00:00:19.876 --> 00:00:25.232
A sheltered staging area may hide the wind or turbulence along the route.

00:00:25.232 --> 00:00:31.000
Inspect launch and recovery surfaces for water, snow, ice, dust, loose debris, mud, slope,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.236
and crew footing.

00:00:32.236 --> 00:00:36.356
Confirm emergency landing areas remain available and that people, vehicles,

00:00:36.356 --> 00:00:39.240
or activity have not changed the plan.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.184
Brief the crew on current conditions, thresholds, route, battery reserve, communication terms,

00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:46.244
landing options, and abort criteria.

00:00:46.244 --> 00:00:49.952
Everyone should understand that raising a concern is expected,

00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:52.424
not an obstacle to mission completion.

00:00:52.424 --> 00:00:54.896
Conditions must be monitored during flight.

00:00:54.896 --> 00:00:59.016
Watch aircraft attitude, groundspeed, battery use, signal, image quality, precipitation,

00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:01.076
visibility, and changing ground activity.

00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:03.960
Trends matter before an alert becomes critical.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.492
If actual conditions differ materially from the plan, pause and reassess.

00:01:08.492 --> 00:01:13.848
A decision made at the office does not obligate the crew to launch.

00:01:13.848 --> 00:01:17.968
Record the final go, delay, modification, or cancellation and why.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.440
Client schedules, travel cost, expiring access,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:24.148
or a waiting crew can create pressure to continue.

00:01:24.148 --> 00:01:30.740
Predefined criteria give the pilot a defensible basis for saying no before that pressure narrows judgment.
